{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And I turn again</b> — when this vision was completed." "<b>And behold four chariots</b> — a chariot [is drawn by] four horses, as written in the book of Kings." "<b>And the meaning of \"between the two mountains\"</b> is concerning the decrees, in the manner of \"and all the host of heaven standing by him, on his right and on his left\" (1 Kings 22:19)." "<b>And bronze</b> — that they stand."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:06.195328152Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}